  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80b439d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. 5-Fold Cross-Validation Evaluation (Option B)\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses all 69 gold tickets in rotation — each fold holds out ~14 for evaluation\n",
    "while the other ~55 are injected as few-shot examples. Aggregating over 5 folds\n",
    "gives the best unbiased estimate of accuracy when using the full gold set in production.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected runtime:** ~3–5 min (5 mini pipeline passes of 14 tickets each)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "644e2a69",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import subprocess, sys, threading\n",
    "\n",
    "_kfold_err: list[str] = []\n",
    "\n",
    "def _cap_kfold_err(proc):\n",
    "    for line in iter(proc.stderr.readline, \"\"):\n",
    "        _kfold_err.append(line)\n",
    "\n",
    "kfold_cmd = [sys.executable, str(PROJECT_DIR / \"scripts\" / \"run_kfold_eval.py\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Starting 5-fold cross-validation...\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "proc_kfold = subprocess.Popen(\n",
    "    kfold_cmd, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\",\n",
    "    stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, bufsize=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "_kt = threading.Thread(target=_cap_kfold_err, args=(proc_kfold,), daemon=True)\n",
    "_kt.start()\n",
    "for _line in iter(proc_kfold.stdout.readline, \"\"):\n",
    "    print(_line, end=\"\", flush=True)\n",
    "proc_kfold.wait()\n",
    "_kt.join(timeout=5)\n",
    "if proc_kfold.returncode != 0 and _kfold_err:\n",
    "    print(\"--- Errors ---\")\n",
    "    print(\"\".join(_kfold_err[-30:]))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Add more corrections to improve accuracy\n",
    "\n",
    "After reviewing the output, add corrections for any misclassified tickets using the FeedbackStore directly. These will be picked up on the next run.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_DIR))\n",
    "from feedback import FeedbackStore\n",
    "\n",
    "store = FeedbackStore(FEEDBACK_DIR)\n",
    "\n",
    "store.add_correction(\n",
    "    module=\"contact_reason\",\n",
    "    uid=\"some_ticket_id\",\n",
    "    text=\"transcript text here...\",\n",
    "    original={\"contact_reason_primary_label\": \"User not able to access\"},\n",
    "    corrected={\"contact_reason_primary_label\": \"Billing\"},\n",
    "    reason=\"The user's main concern was the charge, not the access itself\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The `reason` field has the highest weight in the `smart` strategy — always fill it in."
